      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=3"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 4,
      "nextPhysical": 5,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "acb1669ed7556086632adf8d6053183be69229bcf788bb69378221f6fd1fd115",
      "renderedSHA256": "acb1669ed7556086632adf8d6053183be69229bcf788bb69378221f6fd1fd115",
      "opening": "He also seized upon Jerusalem, and for that end made use of deceit and treachery; for as he came int",
      "closing": " day they were at rest and quietness; and when he had gained it, he ruled over it in a cruel manner.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "13937b0af849c69fd50234dd2faba14ad80a0cc8db038cae9adab9c756f26fc1",
      "greekSHA256": "daad55b736879e325b9871795886425445ae04245fe27a3976a8752ea6b84b8b",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=4"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 5,
      "nextPhysical": 6,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "bd7f9c0614a0f711bb4757b6d34e142d42925247b942f7c4515e9da4d6aaeb8b",
      "renderedSHA256": "bd7f9c0614a0f711bb4757b6d34e142d42925247b942f7c4515e9da4d6aaeb8b",
      "opening": "Nay, Agatharchides of Cnidus, who wrote the acts of Alexander's successors, reproaches us with super",
      "closing": "cessors, reproaches us with superstition, as if we, by it, had lost our liberty; where he says thus:",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "6843b685a4c87d7c0ff2bb3f1991c706ca39564fa7e3faa5d1f166623a529849",
      "greekSHA256": "168c577472c1dec26b0e064c2b2dc9b9fdc6b9db517f2bd175b4bcff44647f94",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=5"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 6,
      "nextPhysical": 7,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "c6c130724ceb00fbe2f3c341a4b4c83c482ef18558a063c119c412015e3f0d8d",
      "renderedSHA256": "c6c130724ceb00fbe2f3c341a4b4c83c482ef18558a063c119c412015e3f0d8d",
      "opening": "\"There is a nation called the nation of the Jews, who inhabit a city strong and great, named Jerusal",
      "closing": "and thereby they submitted to be under a hard master, by reason of their unseasonable superstition.\"",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "d23111224a685979ba44063ca16f3b2c87ac7b8c46da3df23a321123b5718c68",
      "greekSHA256": "e82475b3910ed8f24317e31c861a34867438e1b50157689ee71a54eda0732301",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=6"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 7,
      "nextPhysical": 8,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "725809f4c5ea38d9eab20ffe89d532748de66f14262e377dd99303f44891447a",
      "renderedSHA256": "725809f4c5ea38d9eab20ffe89d532748de66f14262e377dd99303f44891447a",
      "opening": "This is what Agatharchides relates of our nation. But when Ptolemy had taken a great many captives, ",
      "closing": "and Samaria, and the places near Mount Gerizzim, he led them all into Egypt, and settled them there.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "bf4e8112c5cb813bfde01a7763e027c1de996ac6e86232291cf87c0629a9c3eb",
      "greekSHA256": "2bf4a4052d68df731aa43e22e1c42bfef24fde8d11dbc215c8adc21e6612ff45",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=7"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 8,
      "nextPhysical": 9,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "5f4d67e7bc69d2fec77f636dd3ef7d32d33930ca4f7bb45d0ec4511572b28d60",
      "renderedSHA256": "5f4d67e7bc69d2fec77f636dd3ef7d32d33930ca4f7bb45d0ec4511572b28d60",
      "opening": "And as he knew that the people of Jerusalem were most faithful in the observation of oaths and coven",
      "closing": "t they would keep their fidelity to the posterity of those who committed these places to their care.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "eb1f569f2a631aaa9eb81a8c16c038442e1604f9cd0479a455a34106dd118e97",
      "greekSHA256": "c32e5022687edb136edc296571324084bf0fd2a1d212f166b144bbae5bbd9590",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=8"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 9,
      "nextPhysical": 10,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "1173729081e61562e3e1ef76b9992b950a0d05b7eab43ef7df4fb02dc42b22cf",
      "renderedSHA256": "1173729081e61562e3e1ef76b9992b950a0d05b7eab43ef7df4fb02dc42b22cf",
      "opening": "Nay, there were not a few other Jews who, of their own accord, went into Egypt, as invited by the go",
      "closing": "n accord, went into Egypt, as invited by the goodness of the soil, and by the liberality of Ptolemy.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "a82d9d856b985ef72459cda378e898c7b8b95cb87a232fc84976e5d64bd19b32",
