      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=9"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 10,
      "nextPhysical": 11,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "91fe00f8716bcd827ef0a64ac57af136bdc4c4d02a8504a1c20fe9f78c47617b",
      "renderedSHA256": "91fe00f8716bcd827ef0a64ac57af136bdc4c4d02a8504a1c20fe9f78c47617b",
      "opening": "However, there were disoders among their posterity, with relation to the Samaritans, on account of t",
      "closing": "eir sacrifices thither; but the Samaritans were resolved that they should be sent to Mount Gerizzim.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "bc19a03126a0a4dc36f5330a75e94dcb154dfedb87c60575ddd192c8341ac3ee",
      "greekSHA256": "e6cf31a5447e471fa0b0497f38b549bbb45ab22a917be1292f26ae7505605b8b",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=10"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 11,
      "nextPhysical": 12,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "f64a1210d35c68d903370ac9115a7e4bc03a9244c96cf171b1ac76d9a16f5cd9",
      "renderedSHA256": "f64a1210d35c68d903370ac9115a7e4bc03a9244c96cf171b1ac76d9a16f5cd9",
      "opening": "WHEN Alexander had reigned twelve years, and after him Ptolemy Soter forty years, Philadelphus then ",
      "closing": "nto Egypt, and were in slavery there, who were a hundred and twenty thousand. The occasion was this:",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "f591b5bbd39383c7104b171ae42886c575aadda84c55a04bdd45f105ca36754e",
      "greekSHA256": "e9336642ec1a7cd2a0914571b2d6fd3c54f270b28386e40fe93b7dcc1fab9765",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=11"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 12,
      "nextPhysical": 13,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "516c7e1f6c9591480fd9f04b0cdb06cea527a24f61f055d0770f0b79d10346bc",
      "renderedSHA256": "516c7e1f6c9591480fd9f04b0cdb06cea527a24f61f055d0770f0b79d10346bc",
      "opening": "Demetrius Phalerius, who was library keeper to the king, was now endeavoring, if it were possible, t",
      "closing": "stly set upon collecting of books,) to which inclination of his Demetrius was zealously subservient.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "924e1e63f23048984285ab57765491aec922e35c108420aef317b2c6aa78eefe",
      "greekSHA256": "60b3e2a345b8d120728691a43a6b8276b3fea8db9c18662ab86a4e46b8ebd0bf",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=12"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 13,
      "nextPhysical": 14,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "92fab094edcee767faac5b521e90d67690dab68acbf4e1e6ec230fc254a699f8",
      "renderedSHA256": "92fab094edcee767faac5b521e90d67690dab68acbf4e1e6ec230fc254a699f8",
      "opening": "And when once Ptolemy asked him how many ten thousands of books he had collected, he replied, that h",
      "closing": "bout twenty times ten thousand; but that, in a little time, he should have fifty times ten thousand.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "b3eb3a72d0838970db4eeee57c218c478d18dd830ff63be271b06d6a4a1a718f",
      "greekSHA256": "eca97899f8d34b77069cdfc89ca92464cbffb94d214741c718c1178a3985aa68",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=13"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 14,
      "nextPhysical": 15,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "94c98f52a2c07ed9c8468adb6e71c6ce934d80a56bab1d4e16d3c7c084a3d297",
      "renderedSHA256": "94c98f52a2c07ed9c8468adb6e71c6ce934d80a56bab1d4e16d3c7c084a3d297",
      "opening": "But be said he had been informed that there were many books of laws among the Jews worthy of inquiri",
      "closing": " a dialect of their own, will cause no small pains in getting them translated into the Greek tongue;",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "2867f034dc34a9b6df8985fdebb4c570b1532b1054aef69ed628c6319fb8759d",
      "greekSHA256": "457667378f82ef4fdd3e1dbdbd93b011a1624c1d21db0e5758c0d4264e62fdf8",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=14"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 15,
      "nextPhysical": 16,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "b994e4f3f5263161ab7a91583c8d5c9bd578079e9d6301a83b0cf7ba52bed3ba",
      "renderedSHA256": "b994e4f3f5263161ab7a91583c8d5c9bd578079e9d6301a83b0cf7ba52bed3ba",
      "opening": "that the character in which they are written seems to be like to that which is the proper character ",
      "closing": "nothing is wanting that is necessary for that purpose, we may have their books also in this library.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "a9b713cc5954ead06f7546fa6eecc35b928fedb4d54aa5682970eab89c364448",
      "greekSHA256": "ca050764a270e2809886ddbce7455ef7f61c8bf81fd693ac1038259170c6fe6c",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=15"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 16,
      "nextPhysical": 17,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "7ea41be8d633dd0340bec8a7cc8d9f0277af7789c6eb868003e7d27076964541",
      "renderedSHA256": "7ea41be8d633dd0340bec8a7cc8d9f0277af7789c6eb868003e7d27076964541",
      "opening": "So the king thought that Demetrius was very zealous to procure him abundance of books, and that he s",
      "closing": "per for him to do; and therefore he wrote to the Jewish high priest, that he should act accordingly.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "b5e198c0c3ccb1819b2b3354f3f9b85abc5b7d08a2487fcf03a26df5825f7791",
      "greekSHA256": "f53556539ce370b4aae575cf1303c60c7d1868b36e59bcf36ffdf7237daf2dcc",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=16"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 17,
      "nextPhysical": 18,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "18cd57fbb4c7abe67273f2aa705338da778b039b6384e83b6b21ad7cf2bc20ad",
      "renderedSHA256": "18cd57fbb4c7abe67273f2aa705338da778b039b6384e83b6b21ad7cf2bc20ad",
      "opening": "Now there was one Aristeus, who was among the king's most intimate friends, and on account of his mo",
      "closing": "nd that before now, to petition the king that he would set all the captive Jews in his kingdom free;",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "77894f2dd61703b7be9c3f523447b6bbd9ee04973aa971d31795310df082e328",
      "greekSHA256": "fe8919d5264372d9c1de55478365b7fc6dafea98d5881b1a4926179bdf159045",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=17"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 18,
      "nextPhysical": 19,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "252709e7f8faee3b44ed23e3af0403c3f901fd5f309531ce71e7854a9a62a2d2",
      "renderedSHA256": "252709e7f8faee3b44ed23e3af0403c3f901fd5f309531ce71e7854a9a62a2d2",
      "opening": "and he thought this to be a convenient opportunity for the making that petition. So he discoursed, i",
      "closing": ", and Andreas, and persuaded them to assist him in what he was going to intercede with the king for.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "fa530e8894c0374e5f2b7fd529d27483b92d740a13e7a4e08e3131b8ffda1071",
      "greekSHA256": "a08f56b2ce94dab4a09814a4193b0ba9e18f447dcd2f93e6acffa566793cbfd7",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=18"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 19,
      "nextPhysical": 20,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "4b66bb7f6bc83fd390e69ee96967b7b9dc6fdeee919e31c038d41f60aba0769e",
      "renderedSHA256": "4b66bb7f6bc83fd390e69ee96967b7b9dc6fdeee919e31c038d41f60aba0769e",
      "opening": "Accordingly Aristeus embraced the same opinion with those that have been before mentioned, and went ",
      "closing": "h those that have been before mentioned, and went to the king, and made the following speech to him:",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "47e239e7bb75829a403fdbaef378dde4daf25629bc743b65f8551860bfb85855",
      "greekSHA256": "a38a1dd209cebe9a3690b4f933ce7182e9101d09fc1b29e467910537df4f2389",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=19"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 20,
      "nextPhysical": 21,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "b502846a388a237d4c664d6e049d50dbdfeb051910444b9e3ada14810556cf29",
      "renderedSHA256": "b502846a388a237d4c664d6e049d50dbdfeb051910444b9e3ada14810556cf29",
      "opening": "\"It is not fit for us, O king, to overlook things hastily, or to deceive ourselves, but to lay the t",
      "closing": "satisfaction, by what means can we do this, while so many of the Jews are now slaves in thy kingdom?",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "aa1a331b451b24385e7d73f187503618c179f451b94ad12f918cd9741f5ec855",
      "greekSHA256": "c4183b02b198eaa91b60633f9972ed97e2016780a19b0e5ec45382e872b44e97",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=20"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 21,
      "nextPhysical": 22,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "c0993a2bd0b12055e371301eb063ca2acc6b109705fb19c5aa7f0391209201ef",
      "renderedSHA256": "c0993a2bd0b12055e371301eb063ca2acc6b109705fb19c5aa7f0391209201ef",
      "opening": "Do thou then what will be agreeable to thy magnanimity, and to thy good nature: free them from the m",
      "closing": "le condition they are in, because that God, who supporteth thy kingdom, was the author of their laws",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "b733d58dbd02a37f1f82991dc2f497cec6f7a99ce86457012b7ced559a6ff37a",
      "greekSHA256": "84fec46447a9c732ba6591def047b60985e3412d885c82bd5d285ef957f15d19",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=21"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 22,
      "nextPhysical": 23,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "6df0d590f6064302bce860f905fb7c2cc22404e17c11ea8dde3b35c7d2121159",
      "renderedSHA256": "6df0d590f6064302bce860f905fb7c2cc22404e17c11ea8dde3b35c7d2121159",
      "opening": "as I have learned by particular inquiry; for both these people, and we also, worship the same God th",
      "closing": "untry, and this do to the honor of God, because these men pay a peculiarly excellent worship to him.",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
      "inline": 0,
      "latinSHA256": "0183d30b6b07b3afe619c6f1135c1f2f10156a7c29d8dfd3c7c1b371501feb08",
      "greekSHA256": "1818ba665d257a46f3dedacb7ebdb2652470a2327e7e037d8c3ac6998c5f2ba8",
      "GreekLatinPresentationUnchanged": true,
      "URL": "?book=12&niese=22"
    },
    {
      "book": "12",
      "number": 23,
      "nextPhysical": 24,
      "passed": true,
      "expectedSHA256": "7a6e74d27d74701a1ab1d41ceecc57a7d78c2541ad52a75338922fcb8a6fedf3",
      "renderedSHA256": "7a6e74d27d74701a1ab1d41ceecc57a7d78c2541ad52a75338922fcb8a6fedf3",
      "opening": "And know this further, that though I be not of kin to them by birth, nor one of the same country wit",
      "closing": "l-pleased with those that do good. I do therefore put up this petition to thee, to do good to them.\"",
      "allNarrativeVisible": true,
      "notes": 0,
